WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.940
For millions of people around the globe, the
Harry Potter book and film series were the

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.560
closest they'd ever come to experiencing actual
magic. The journey of the young wizard, from

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.550
an orphan who lived under the stairs at his
cruel aunt's home into the legendary hero

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.980
who defeated the world's darkest villain,
was nothing short of epic.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.860
The final installment of the story was as
complex as it needed to be to wrap up seven

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.029
chapters' worth of sorcerer storytelling.
So, to make sure you caught everything important

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:27.970
at the end, let's shed a little lumos light
on what happened in the conclusion to the

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.890
Harry Potter saga.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.240
"Wicked!"

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.079
Snape's true side comes through

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:38.780
In the beginning of the final film, dementors
loomed over Hogwarts. Professor Snape observed

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.850
from on high how much devastation the Dark
Lord's looming presence had caused his school.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.559
But he had to carry on because it was all
part of the plan no one else knew about.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:50.429
See, Snape might've seemed like a terrible
person throughout the whole series, but his

00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:54.600
true loyalties became clear in his final moments.
He was ultimately expelled from school and

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.710
killed by Voldemort's snake, just so the Dark
Lord could take true ownership of the Elder

00:00:58.710 --> 00:00:59.710
Wand.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.120
Some friend Voldy was.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.790
Harry overheard everything and tried to rush
in and help Snape as soon as You Know Who

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.700
was gone, but it was too late. Instead, Snape
used his last moments to give his least favorite

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.830
student a teardrop full of memories.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.860
In them, Harry discovered the gut-wrenching
backstory of Snape's unrequited love for Harry's

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.040
mother Lily.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.980
"After all this time?"

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:23.640
"Always."

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.220
As it turned out, he'd been crazy about her
since childhood and was also looking after

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:31.320
Harry the whole time by feigning allegiance
to the Dark Lord. The only reason he murdered

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.439
Dumbledore was because the headmaster was
already dying and didn't want Draco Malfoy

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:36.930
to be forced to do the deed.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.860
Snape's open contempt for Harry at Hogwarts
was still pretty real, since he looked so

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.229
much like his dad James, but he was trying
to protect Harry all the while so he could

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:47.909
fulfill his destiny to defeat the Dark Lord.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:51.229
It probably didn't hurt Snape's feelings too
much that Harry Potter was always meant to

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:55.000
die in his big battle with Voldemort, though.
Speaking of which…

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.149
No Resurrection Stone required

00:01:57.149 --> 00:02:01.180
There's a reason Dumbledore had his eye on
Harry Potter from day one and helped fan the

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.109
flames on Harry's "chosen one" persona in
the wizarding community. He was one of the

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:09.330
few people who knew that Harry was predestined
to die in a battle against Voldemort.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.180
"You have the grim."

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:17.400
Harry finally realized the truth about his
fate once he saw Snape's memories and found

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.900
he out he himself was the final horcrux.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:26.040
"A part of Voldemort lives inside him."

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:31.980
After Helga Hufflepuff's cup was destroyed,
and the Diadem of Rowena Ravenclaw was done

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.800
for, Harry left Hermione and Ron to deal with
the snake while he set off on what he knew

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.010
was a suicide mission to face Voldemort in
the Forbidden Forest.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.400
"So when the time comes the boy must die?"

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:47.620
"Yes."

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:51.709
He didn't exactly know what would happen after
that, of course, but he trusted the late headmaster

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:54.920
enough to follow his lead, even to his own
death if necessary.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:02.840
"The Boy Who Lived, come to die."

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.190
Upon going gently into that good night, Harry
awakened in what appeared to be a milky white

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:12.629
vision of King's Cross Station, where he'd
hopped onto Platform 9¾ so many times before.

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:16.580
Dumbledore awaited him with news that he'd
successfully killed off the part of Voldemort

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.580
that remained inside of him in the process
of dying. So, Harry had a choice to board

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:25.040
a train back to the realm of the living or
to just move on … to where, he didn't say.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.360
Harry, knowing his battle wasn't done, opted
for the former. He left behind the scaly,

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.569
tiny version of Voldemort that had infected
his mind for so long, and used his perceived

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.439
death to gain an advantage. Hagrid carried
him back to the school just as an unknowing

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:42.080
Voldemort started bragging about his conquest
to garner new recruits — and got an unexpected

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.290
surprise.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.599
The Elder Wand was his all along

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:49.300
No matter how many horcruxes Harry and his
friends successfully destroyed, Voldemort

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.939
was still a more powerful wizard than all
of them. So, when Harry arose from the dead

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:57.579
to pick a final fight with the Dark Lord,
he was very quickly overtaken by You-Know-Who.

00:03:57.579 --> 00:04:01.379
But Voldemort still couldn't kill him with
the wand again, even after he'd taken ownership

00:04:01.379 --> 00:04:05.260
from Snape. Why? Well, it turned out that
Snape wasn't the one who'd gained control

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.680
of the Elder Wand in the first place, so it
didn't actually pass to Voldemort upon Snape's

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:10.680
execution.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.380
While Snape had indeed killed Dumbledore and
taken possession of the wand in Half-Blood

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.690
Prince, it was Draco who'd originally disarmed
Dumbledore, and thus received the allegiance

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:23.390
of the Elder Wand. Then, when Harry disarmed
him in their subsequent duel, it was Harry

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.020
who'd laid claim to the Elder Wand.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.890
So, while the Elder Wand was successfully
used to strike its master down in the forest

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.650
— when Harry had surrendered himself to
the Dark Lord — he still wasn't disarmed

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:36.690
of the wand in that battle. It remained loyal
to Harry, instead of Voldemort. And it wasn't

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:40.320
the only magical instrument that came into
play to take ol' Snakeface down.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.790
A key weapon presented itself

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:47.150
The Sword of Gryffindor had been an instrumental
tool in destroying horcruxes throughout Harry

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:51.250
Potter lore. Dumbledore used it to destroy
the Gaunt family ring. Harry retrieved it

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:55.790
from the frozen lake, and Ron used it to destroy
the locket that was causing his buddy so much

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:00.030
mental anguish. Despite knowing its powers,
Harry offered the sword to Griphook in exchange

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:03.880
for his help to get them into Bellatrix Lestrange's
vault at Gringotts.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:07.050
Griphook returned to villainy soon after,
though, and left Harry and his friends in

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.570
the lurch by abandoning them in the vault
caverns with no promise to get them out. Hermione,

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:15.880
always with a clever idea up her sleeve, led
the trio to ride a dungeon-bound dragon out

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.540
of the bank, with Griphook perishing in the
fiery skirmish that ensued.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.120
"That's unfortunate."

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.510
The sword then disappeared from his grip,
to present itself to a more worthy pair of

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.510
hands.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.510
"That was brilliant. Absolutely brilliant."

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.300
Later on, when Hermione and Ron were back
at Hogwarts trying to lure Nagini away, the

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:33.060
Sword presented itself to Neville Longbottom
so he could slice the snake's head off and

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:37.380
deal Voldemort one last crucial blow as he
fought his ultimate battle with Harry.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:41.091
Unlike other similar weapons in the Harry
Potter-verse, the Sword knew no master, and

00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:45.720
simply chose whoever was worthiest at the
time. And few were more worthy than Neville.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.710
"People die every day!"

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:57.060
"He didn't die in vain. But you will."

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:02.030
After that, the Elder Wand returned to Harry
and left Voldemort falling to pieces. Literally.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.960
The Deathly Hallows come together at last

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:08.331
There was an interesting Easter egg contained
in Harry's first shot of the last film. As

00:06:08.331 --> 00:06:12.460
he mourned Dobby's beachfront grave, he looked
in a triangular fragment of a mirror the elf

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.620
had possessed. Thanks to the circular nature
of his glasses, it created the symbol of the

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.310
Deathly Hallows in the reflection as a wink
to how all three elements would eventually

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.310
be his.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.280
As explained in The Tale of the Three Brothers
in the second-to-last movie, the Deathly Hallows

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.270
consisted of the Elder Wand, the Cloak of
Invisibility, and the Resurrection Stone.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:33.870
When combined, they gave a wizard untold power,
the ability to disappear from Death's purview,

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.680
and a means to bring back lost souls. Voldemort
got his hands on one — the Elder Wand — while

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:42.520
Harry had been casually given the cloak in
his earliest days at Hogwarts, not knowing

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:46.490
its strength. He eventually recovered the
Stone, too, after kissing his Snitch goodbye

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.990
with the intention of sacrificing himself.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:53.120
Unlike Voldemort, however, Harry didn't aim
to use these items for world domination once

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.210
he came into possession of all three. Instead,
he snapped the Elder Wand in half and dropped

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:01.470
the Resurrection Stone in the Forbidden Forest
to be trampled into the dirt by a centaur.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:05.290
He did keep the cloak for himself because,
it had once belonged to his late father — and

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:09.720
who'd give up an invisibility cloak? He'd
later pass the Cloak down to his own son,

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:13.260
James Sirius Potter — and James' younger
brother, Albus Severus, who would later swipe

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.050
it in the events of The Cursed Child.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:16.710
Speaking of which …

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.410
The next generation

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:22.680
In the 19-years-ahead epilogue to Deathly
Hallows, we met Harry Potter's trio of children

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:27.720
with Ginny Weasley. Particular attention was
paid to Albus Severus Potter, his second son,

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:31.680
as he prepared to board the Hogwarts Express
for his start at the school. The boy was contending

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:35.520
with the possibility that he might not make
it into Gryffindor, and Harry consoled him

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.520
as best he could.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.650
"Let's just say that I am."

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:43.830
"Then Slytherin house will have gained a wonderful
young wizard."

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:47.110
Little did we know at the time of this movie's
release release, but this was ushering in

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:51.400
a new generation of wizarding journeys, which
plays out on the stage in Rowling's Harry

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.000
Potter and the Cursed Child.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.580
Was it all in his head?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:58.300
There's a popular fan theory that everything
that happened to Harry Potter outside of Privet

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:02.740
Drive was a mental making of his young, abused
mind, and Deathly Hallows did little to dispel

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:03.740
that theory.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:07.020
In fact, the movies seemed to give a wink
to that possibility by having Harry ask his

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.410
late Professor if his crazy adventure was
all just happening in his head.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:16.680
"Of course it's happening inside your head
Harry. Why should that mean that it's not

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.680
real?"

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.820
So, was the entirety of the Harry Potter universe
fiction coming from the imagination of a desperate

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.700
boy who lived under the stairs and who wished
for something more?

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:29.090
"Actually if I think about it, it doesn't
seem curious at all."

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:32.640
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.610
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

